When dereferencing array fields from the input closeout payload, use Array.isArray to safely default to an empty array and trigger a validation failure if the field is present but is not an array. This ensures the validator fails closed gracefully instead of throwing a TypeError.

```javascript
  const inventory = c.artifact_inventory ?? {};
  const issues = Array.isArray(c.live_issue_pr_map?.issues) ? c.live_issue_pr_map.issues : [];
  if (c.live_issue_pr_map?.issues !== undefined && !Array.isArray(c.live_issue_pr_map.issues)) {
    errors.push('live_issue_pr_map_issues_not_an_array');
  }
  const validators = c.upstream_validator_statuses ?? {};
  const gates = Array.isArray(c.future_authorization_gates) ? c.future_authorization_gates : [];
  if (c.future_authorization_gates !== undefined && !Array.isArray(c.future_authorization_gates)) {
    errors.push('future_authorization_gates_not_an_array');
